 Research Scientist","gender":"female","division":"Zone 2: Academic Research Wing","animation_state":"research","accent_color":"#c084fc","plumbob_color":"#38bdf8","speech_bubble":"Research Paper: Precise Rotation Sequencing in Python AVL Trees: A Step-by-Step Analysis of All Four Cases","headline":"Precise Rotation Sequencing in Python AVL Trees: A Step-by-Step Analysis of All Four Cases","paper_topic":"Precise Rotation Sequencing in Python AVL Trees: A Step-by-Step Analysis of All Four Cases","author":"Mateus Yonathan","language":"Python","timestamp_wib":"30 October 2026, 21:04 WIB","metadata":{"Scientist Name":"Dr. Clara Wijaya","Research Paper":"Precise Rotation Sequencing in Python AVL Trees: A Step-by-Step Analysis of All Four Cases","Research Domain":"AVL Tree Rotations Explained Step by Step (With All 4 Cases)","Primary Language":"Python","Published (WIB)":"30 October 2026, 21:04 WIB","Published Papers":"114"},"abstract":"AVL trees maintain strict height balance through rotations, guaranteeing logarithmic search, insertion, and deletion times. This work presents a detailed, step-by-step exposition of all four rotation cases—single left, single right, left-right, and right-left—implemented in pure Python. We formalize the height-balance invariant, prove its preservation under each rotation, and provide a concise algorithmic description that can be directly mapped to the source code in the public repository. Empirical evaluation in our research evaluation environment,.20 µs and a throughput of 20 085 ops/s over 30 benchmark iterations.","proof_lines":["[1] AVL trees maintain strict height balance through rotations, guaranteeing logarithmic search, insertion, and deletion times.","[2] This work presents a detailed, step-by-step exposition of all four rotation cases—single left, single right, left-right, and right-left—implemented in pure Python.","[3] We formalize the height-balance invariant, prove its preservation under each rotation, and provide a concise algorithmic description that can be directly mapped to the source code in the public repository.","[4] Empirical evaluation in our research evaluation environment,.20 µs and a throughput of 20 085 ops/s over 30 benchmark iterations."],"preview_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/myonathanlinkedin/mini-papers/main/papers/2026-10-30_avl_tree_rotations_explained_step_b/debug_pages/page_1.png","recent_items":[{"id":"2026-10-30_avl_tree_rotations_explained_step_b","title":"Precise Rotation Sequencing in Python AVL Trees: A Step-by-Step Analysis of All Four Cases","topic":"AVL Tree Rotations Explained Step by Step (With All 4 Cases)","language":"Python","published_wib":"30 October 2026, 21:04 WIB","preview_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/myonathanlinkedin/mini-papers/main/papers/2026-10-30_avl_tree_rotations_explained_step_b/debug_pages/page_1.png","scholar_url":"https://myonathanlinkedin.github.io/papers/2026-10-30_avl_tree_rotations_explained_step_b/"},{"id":"2026-10-30_on_zeros_and_algorithms_for_disorde","title":"On Zeros and Algorithms for Disordered Systems II: Runtime Invariants and Algorithmic Bounds in Python","topic":"On Zeros and Algorithms for Disordered Systems II: The Antiferromagnetic Ising Model up","language":"Python","published_wib":"30 October 2026, 18:04 WIB","preview_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/myonathanlinkedin/mini-papers/main/papers/2026-10-30_on_zeros_and_algorithms_for_disorde/debug_pages/page_1.png","scholar_url":"https://myonathanlinkedin.github.io/papers/2026-10-30_on_zeros_and_algorithms_for_disorde/"},{"id":"2026-10-30_a_case_study_of_a_multi_agent_kerne","title":"Height-Balanced Invariant Preservation and Latency Bounds in a Python Aether-Vector Stratum-Optimizer Loop","topic":"A Case Study of a High-Performance Systems Architecture That Learns a New AI Accelerator","language":"Python","published_wib":"30 October 2026, 12:03 WIB","preview_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/myonathanlinkedin/mini-papers/main/papers/